NEARS-3639 / NEARS-3701 — cycle-2 delta re-QA (sha cf5695a09, emulator-5556,
English locale, live device, logged-in as sophie.davis@demo.com).

CLAIM UNDER TEST (fix-cycle packet): "Re-run the SAME live a11y dump ... confirm
exactly ONE node per row now (not two)."

RESULT: NOT CONFIRMED. Order-updates / Offers-promotions rows still expose TWO
distinct, independently-focusable accessibility nodes at identical bounds — the
specific ROOT CAUSE changed, the симптом (2 nodes) did not.

Evidence file: docs/qa-evidence/NEARS-3639/NEARS-3701-settings-a11y-dump.xml
(live uiautomator dump, pulled this run, both rows checked=true — a second dump
after toggling Offers off is in the run notes, confirming toggled/checked state
correctly flips on the OUTER node only).

Extract, "Order updates" row (bounds [96,1001][1248,1193]):

<node class="android.widget.Switch" content-desc="Order updates, switch"
      checkable="true" checked="true" clickable="true" focusable="true"
      bounds="[96,1001][1248,1193]">
  <node class="android.view.View" content-desc="Order updates"
        checkable="false" clickable="true" focusable="true"
        bounds="[96,1001][1248,1193]" />
</node>

Same shape for "Offers & promotions" (bounds [96,1194][1248,1386]).

WHAT IS FIXED (verified, do not re-litigate): the cycle-1 defect was the
trailing NSwitch's own baked `Semantics(toggled:)` node competing with the row
(cycle-1 evidence: bug-order-updates-row-doubled-a11y-node.log — a NESTED
`android.widget.Switch` class node, itself checkable=true/checked=true, one
level BELOW an intermediate View). That inner Switch-classed duplicate is GONE.
`_switchTrailing()`'s `ExcludeSemantics(child: switchWidget)` (n_settings_tile.dart,
NEARS-3701 comment) removed it, and `toggled: _trailingSwitchValue` on the OUTER
`Semantics(container:true, explicitChildNodes:true, ...)` now correctly carries
the real on/off state — confirmed live: toggling "Offers & promotions" off via
its row tap flips the OUTER node's `checked` from `true` to `false` and back
when toggled again (re-dumped both times), single source of truth. Widget test
`setting_page_notification_split_test.dart` "...merge into exactly one toggled
semantics node..." also reflects this correctly — but note its predicate is
narrower than the AC: it walks the tree and asserts exactly one node carries
`SemanticsData.flagsCollection.isToggled != null`, which is now true (1 toggled
node), but it does NOT count total nodes with a label/action under the row —
so it cannot see the second, non-toggled node below. Green here does not mean
"1 node total".

WHAT IS STILL BROKEN: a SECOND node persists, now sourced differently. Root
cause (packages/nears_dls/lib/elements/settings_tile/n_settings_tile.dart,
buildContent()): the row's own `InkWell(onTap: onTap, ...)` is used bare, with
no `excludeFromSemantics` param passed. Per Flutter's own
`ink_well.dart` (~line 1401), InkWell always wraps its child in its own
`Semantics(onTap: simulateTap)` node (no `container:true` on that node). Under
the OUTER `explicitChildNodes: true` boundary added by this ticket, that
InkWell node can no longer merge upward, so it survives as its own explicit
child — and since it has no container boundary of its own, it in turn absorbs
the (non-excluded) label Text underneath it, producing the plain-label,
non-checkable "Order updates" node seen above, at the SAME bounds as the whole
row (the InkWell fills the row).

This is exactly the shape THIS SAME DESIGN SYSTEM already solved elsewhere:
`NSurfaceCard.excludeInkSemantics` (packages/nears_dls/lib/elements/surface_card/
n_surface_card.dart:57,78,208) forwards straight to the native
`InkWell(excludeFromSemantics: ...)` parameter, and is already wired at every
other row-with-a-merged-semantic-label call site in this DLS:
  - n_active_order_banner.dart:70  excludeInkSemantics: onTap != null && semanticLabel != null
  - n_item_card.dart:323,347,511   (same predicate)
  - n_reorder_shortcut_card.dart:185
NSettingsTile's own `InkWell` in buildContent() is the ONLY row-shaped element
in this file set that never received the equivalent treatment — it builds a
bare `InkWell` directly rather than routing through NSurfaceCard, so there is
no existing prop to flip; the fix is either (a) pass
`excludeFromSemantics: semanticLabel != null` directly on that InkWell
(mirrors the NActiveOrderBanner predicate exactly), or (b) rebuild the row on
NSurfaceCard and use `excludeInkSemantics` for parity with the rest of the DLS.

Positive control (proves the instrument/dump was live, not empty): the same
dump's "About Us" row (index 9, no semanticLabel set — setting_page.dart passes
none for that row) is a SINGLE self-closing node, content-desc="About Us",
clickable=true, no nested children — confirms rows WITHOUT the
container+explicitChildNodes wrapper merge cleanly into exactly one node by
Flutter's default semantics behavior, and that this uiautomator dump correctly
distinguishes 1-node rows from 2-node rows in the same screen, same dump.

Net: NEARS-3701 AC ("exactly one node per row") is not yet met. Recommend one
more fix-cycle: add `excludeFromSemantics: semanticLabel != null` (or route via
NSurfaceCard) to NSettingsTile's InkWell.
